<title>USA: U.S. Dec industrial output rose 0.8 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Dec industrial output rose 0.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Board report of U.S. industrial production and capacity utilization, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p> Total Industrial:	  Dec    Nov    Oct   Sept   Dec96/95</p>
<p> Production, Pct Change   0.8    0.8   -0.1    0.2    5.1</p>
<p> Previous Estimates		  0.9   -0.2    0.1</p>
<p> Production Index-X     129.1  128.1  127.1  127.2</p>
<p> -				Dec    Nov    Oct   Sept   Dec95</p>
<p> Pct of Capacity Use     83.8   83.4    83.0  83.4   82.9</p>
<p> Previous Estimates		 83.3   82.9   83.3</p>
<p>X--1987 equals 100.  </p>
<p>Industrial Production,Seasonally adjusted percent changes:</p>
<p> -				Dec    Nov    Oct   Sept  Dec96/95</p>
<p> Major Market Products    0.6    1.0   UNCH    0.4    5.1</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods	    0.5    1.2   -0.1    0.3    2.6</p>
<p> -Business Equipment	1.1    1.2    0.3    0.6   11.5</p>
<p> -Construc.Supplies	 0.5    1.2   -1.3    0.8    4.8</p>
<p> Major Materials	    0.9    0.5   -0.2   -0.1    5.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing Industry   1.1    0.7   -0.1    0.3    5.6</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	     1.3    0.9   -0.5    UNCH   7.3</p>
<p> --Primary Metals	   2.9   -4.6    2.5    0.7    1.4</p>
<p> --Autos/Light Trucks     0.5    7.5   -8.1   -3.2    2.9</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods	 0.8    0.5    0.5    0.7    3.4</p>
<p> --Petroleum Products     0.6   -1.6    1.6   -0.8    2.3</p>
<p> Mining Industry	    1.2    0.6    0.1   -0.8    5.9</p>
<p> Utilities Industry	-3.3    2.3    0.1   -0.1   -0.8</p>
<p>Percent of Capacity: Manufacturing, Mining, Utilities:</p>
<p>    (Seasonally Adj.)     Dec    Nov    Oct   Sept   Dec'95</p>
<p> Manufacturing	     82.8   82.2   81.9   82.3   81.9</p>
<p>Percent of Capacity: Manufacturing, Mining, Utilities:</p>
<p>    (Seasonally Adj.)     Dec    Nov    Oct   Sept   Dec'95</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	    82.2   81.6   81.3   82.2   81.7</p>
<p> --Primary Metals	  91.0   88.6   93.1   91.1   92.6</p>
<p> --Autos/Light Trucks    82.3   81.9   76.4   83.2   81.2</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods	83.5   83.0   82.7   82.4   82.1</p>
<p> --Petroleum Products    94.7   94.1   95.7   94.2   93.3</p>
<p> Mining			93.0   91.9   91.3   91.2   87.7</p>
<p> Utilities		   90.2   93.4   91.4   91.4   92.2</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected December industrial production to rise 0.6 percent from November and estimated that December capacity use would be at a rate of 83.5 percent.</p>
<p>The Fed said that the December capacity use rate of 83.8 percent was the highest since August 1995 when it was at 83.9 percent.</p>
<p>Unseasonably mild weather in December caused a large drop in utilities output, the Fed said, which reduced the growth rate of overall production by about 0.3 percentage point.</p>
<p>Motor vehicle assemblies rose in December to a rate of 5.8 million a year for cars from 6.1 million in November. For light trucks the assembly rate was up to 6 million from 5.6 million.</p>
